: I am looking for Dec Alpha Luggable (basically a PC AT or ATX case with LCD
: stuck on it).  I want to run Windows NT and ProENGINEER on it and take it
: to client sites.  Does anybody know of a manufacturer that does this?  Or
: Intel Luggable that could take a Alpha motherboard?

IIRC, there were at least some of the luggables that could take a standard
"Baby-AT" size motherboard. So, you could try getting a "Noname" (AXPpci)
motherboard and put that in. The Noname board is available with an AXP21066
CPU at 166 or 233 MHz.

The biggest problem is getting the LC display to work. Some luggables had a 
VGA-compatible card for an ISA slot which may or may not work; some seem to
have a VGA->LCD adapter board, so you could use any VGA board you like.

