		http://www.sccs.org/isscc/1997/ap/FA10.htm
	
	for *some* detail.  At the same URL we learn the 21264 will be a 
	40 SpecInt95 and 60 SpecFp95 part.  P7/Merced will come in
	at 40 SpecInt95 at the end of 1998, early 1999.  Seems to me
	Digital will have at least an 18 month performance lead.
	
	The 21164PC is a 1Q97 volume CPU.  When can we expect Exponential?
	How will a $1000 Exponential part compete on the low-end with
	a $400 dollar 21164PC part?  It won't.  The 21164PC will be in
	under $3000 PC's by 1Q97.  Can't say the same for the Exponential
	part.

				Rob





