That's because you'd have to understand the kernel before rewritting it.
You can change VMS, but you have to know what you're doing.  It was 
built such that someone with no knowledge of the underlying OS would have 
a hard time screwing it up.  Plenty of people that have proper training
create products for VMS that diddle with the internals; cachers, system 
tuners, memory tuners, I/O intercepters, etc.  Deploying these products
