	Yes they will *eventually* catch up to early 1997.

	Digital in conjunction with Mitsubishi is getting ready to ship 21164PC
	parts which will allow a < $3000 PC that does 14 SpecInt95
	and 17 SpecFp95.  Cull dejanews or altavista for Burkhard's
	analysis of this if interested.  

	So, the question to ask is:

		"When will Sun ship a < $4000 workstation that does > 12
		 SpecInt95?"

	Not any time soon.  Can't really speculate on it because as far
	as I can tell Sun isn't even talking about such a box.

	Follow-up question:

		"When Sun eventually reaches a price-performance point that 
		 Digital is/will be at, where will Digital be?"

	Good question.  Probably a year ahead still.  Meaning 21264 begins
	to move and Samsung second sourcing, look for lower costing 21264 
	parts and Sun once again has to go up against a much more powerful 
	part that will invade the $7000 to $10000 market in a year.

	Realize Digital and friends in early '97 will be shipping PC's
	running NT that smoke any Sun box.  A wonderful marketing opportunity:

		"Our PCs smoke your workstations, IF you want to see what
		 a REAL workstation is you have to saddle up a 21264 based-
		 machine."

	Sun marketing is sweating bullets even as we speak.

