	Digital has never before had performance *dominance*.  Terry points
	out that 21264 may be 40 int, 60 fp.  Not unreasonable considering
	at 500 MHz is 30+ SpecInt95 (from MicroProcessor Forum).  If Digital
	ships a 600+ MHz 21264 and tweeks compilers, etc.  40 or near 40 
	wouldn't be unreasonable.  Digital always sandbags a bit on numbers 
	when they kick them around anyhow.

	Think about it.  Put yourself in the shoes of a high-end workstation
	purchaser ( $35000 or higher ).  You can look at a 12 SpecInt95,
	20 SpecFp95 HP box.  Very nice.  A ~8 SpecInt95 12? SpecFp95 Sun
