In article <59apd1$19e@edward.redted.demon.co.uk>, Kevan <kevan@redted.demon.co.uk> writes:

:I have just recently acquired a VAX 3100 M76 for my computer collection.
:Unfortunately it does not come with a monitor (it has an SPX graphics card)
:so I would like to connect a terminal to it, to see if it boots etc.
:Could someone tell me the pin-outs for the serial port so I can make up a
:cable.

   The MMJ comm port pinout is in the OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions
   (FAQ) -- it's the standard MMJ pinout.  Copies of the FAQ available at:

       ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/vms
       ftp://rtfm.mit.edu/pub/usenet/news.answers/dec-faq/vms

   Be aware that the VAXstation 3100 MMJ comm port does not have modem
   control.

: Pin-outs for the video connector would be nice also as I may be 
:able to find a monitor to use with it.

  What you likely want are the part numbers for the cable or a used
  (salvaged) cable, not the pinouts -- video signals don't work well
  with most home-made cables.  You will also need a very specific
  monitor for the SPX, specifically one that accepts video at 1280 x
  1024 x 66 Hz with -- and this is the tricky part -- a synch-on-green
  RGB BNC connection.   Monitors: VR319 (mono), VR320 (color), VRT19
  (color), etc.  The SPX also supported a lower-resolution, 1024 x 864
  x 60 Hz, again, a synch-on-green RGB BNC connection.  Monitors: VR160,
  VR297, VR299 (all color), etc.

  The BC23J-03 was the standard video cable used for this box.

