  The RRD42 uses regular ("normal") CD caddys which you should be able to get
from your local computer store or mail order catalog outfit (PC Connection,
INMAC, etc.).

  The RRD40 used the proprietary LMS caddy which nobody else used. It's the
one where the disc is held between 2 pieces of plastic that look like insect
mandibles and there's a plastic cover that comes off when the CD is inserted
in the drive.

  Oh, and the RRD50 was a caddy-less LMS drive. I think all of the newer RRD
units are caddy-less as well.

