Ron K. wrote:
> 
> I have a Starion 911 with onboard S3 video.  I added a Matrox Millennium
> card and disabled the S3 in the Device Manager.  Whenever I remove the
> S3 drivers, W95 tries to reinstall them when I reboot Windows.  Steve
> Lionel has assured me that there is no conflict between the cards, but I
> still wonder if this is the reason why I can't get the Color Controls
> option from Matrox to work in Display Manager.  Email me with any
> suggestions or experiences.

When you disable or remove the S3 select from Device Manager, the next
time you boot, Win95 will find the device (its listed in the BIOS even
though its disabled) and attempt to load the drivers. Once Win95 is
running, its will discover that the device is disabled and should report
that in Device manager (you should see a yellow exclaimation mark next
to the device). At this point if you examine the properties for the
device you should see that the device is listed as diabled. Leave it
alone at this point and do not attempt to remove. Now load the Maxtrox
drivers and once you re-boot you should be able to use all the functions
of the Matrox controls.

regards,

glen kelley
digital



