: Hi. I just found a few VaxStations 2000, almost all of them are dead. 

What are the exact symptoms ?

: I want to bring up at least one working. So, I have a question: how much 
: maximum memory can afford this machine ? 

14 MB. You have 2 MB on-board and can add a memory expansion board with up to
12 MB RAM. There is also a third-party-board that provides additional 14 MB,
but this requires exchanging the VaxStation's boot PROMs with speical ones.

: What is the maximum hdd sizes ? 

170 MB (RD54). In theory, any MFM hard disk will do. Some people use old
ST251's from 286AT systems (40 MB), which work just fine. You can also 
connect a standard 5.25" floppy disk (1.2 MB HD) from a PC, just make sure
you set the drive select jumper to drive 0 (1 is PC standard :-().

You can format MFM hard disks by issuing the command
>>> T 70
from the boot monitor prompt.

: Which software can I run on it (in meantime, I want to get Ultrix 4.? 
: working and any of the old VMS) ? 

Ultrix 4.x works, I have 4.3 running on one of my VS2000 here. Some version of
VMS also works, the VS2000's were used as X-terminals with VMS here ...

: Can I run X11R6 on it ? 

Don't know if the VS2000 frame buffer is supported in X11R6.

: Is it slow ? 

One word : YES !

: How does it compares to Intel-series machines ? 

Hmmm, hard to say. Perhaps comparable to a 25 MHz 386 or so.

: What I should know, when I will compile at least one crate from those? 

There are more screws than you'd expect :-). Nothing really special about
the VS2000, though. If you get into problems, email me.

: Which hardware is better ? Is there a NetBSD version that I can run on it ? 

There is a NetBSD version for the VS2000 in development, but there are no 
binary distributions (boot disks etc.) so far.

: Which Ultrix is better for this crate - 3.x or 4.x or maybe even 4.5 ?

4.3 runs fine. Be sure to use a version the takes up as less disk space as
possible !

: Please, help me to solve this problem! :)

Hope this helps,
regards,
