The FR-PCXAG-AL takes plain and simple 256x16 60 ns. SOJs, so the
brand does not matter.  I have not seen the FR-PC77M-DA kit, but I did
sell over 100 surplus FR-PC77M-CA 1MB kits, and they contained NOTHING
EXCEPT the chips.  Not even fancy wrappings.

I think that there is a software issue here, not a hardware one.  NT
is not known for the breadth of its software driver support,
especially those that are shipped in the box.  You may not be able to
use the card to its fullest with NT.  Not sure what you mean by "VESA
in DOS crashes the system."  Check with S3's web site,
