>Jeez, I guess I've been lucky so far. I have an early Starion 700 (Pentium
>90).
>According to Wintune, it runs just a hair behind the Centrex P90, which is
>supposed to be on of the fastest ones around. My disk is slow (Western
>Digital 730) and the video is a little on the slow side, even after I
>upgraded
>it to 2mb video memory.
>
>I do have a weird problem with upgrading the main memory. It comes with
>8mb hard-wired to the motherboard. I upgraded it with 2 16mb simm's, but
>it
>only recognizes one of them, for a total of 24mb, when it should see 40mb.
>I thought one of the simm's was faulty, so I exchanged them for two
>others,
>but I still have the problem. They're EDO, but that shouldn't make a
>difference.
>Any ideas?

Many PC compatibles expect any additional memory chips in the second bank
to be equal or smaller than the first bank, thus treating your 2 16mb
simms as 2 8mb simms.

Is it possible to switch the two sets of simms, or is the first 2 8mb
simms soldered dowm? If you can, I'll bet you'll see the full memory.




