I have seen other problems similar to this with a SCSI chain that is
on the verge of being too long... If you connect another device to
your chain (instead of the HP) to give it the same number of devices
you had with the HP, do you still have problems?  Another thing you
might look at is the uerf (event report formatter) to see if you are
getting CAM SCSI errors (another indicator of SCSI chain/device
problems):

uerf -R |more

This will list them in reverse order (most recent first).  If you see
a large number of CAM errors, you might want to try shortening the
chain (i.e. use shorter length cables or better shielded ones)...

