In article <59b0f8$svg@cobweb.microweb.com> mib@microweb.com (Josiah J Fizer) writes:
> Is there a way to use a third party video card on a multi alpha system?

Yes, on a Multia with a 2.5 inch internal disk (or no internal disk), most
any VGA compatible PCI card that is short enough to fit will work.  Models
with a 3.5 inch internal disk do not have a PCI expansion slot.

The SRM and ARC console firmware and Windows NT should all automatically
use the VGA card instead of the on-board TGA.

However, if you are running Linux, you will need to build Milo and the kernel
with VGA support, and the kernel should be built *without* TGA support.  The
kernel assumes that if a TGA is present that it should be the console.

Cheers,
Eric
