Or perhaps it indicates that the PPC coalition saw no chance of
matching Alpha speeds over the long run.  The "safe" bet for NT
customers is to stick with Intel, so perhaps those who go out on
a limb for RISC will always choose the fastest.

One thing PPC has going for it, however, is Macintosh, and the
number of people who might want a dual-boot machine between
Macintosh and NT certainly exceeds those who want dual-boot
between VMS and NT.

But the Motorola and IBM statements do not say that Windows NT
will not _run_ on PPC in the future, just that Motorola and IBM
will not be doing the software work.  They might have seen that
effort as just subsidizing Microsoft.  The former MIPS Windows NT
support was financed by Microsoft as I heard it. While Motorola
and IBM are larger companies than Microsoft, a lot of that is
due to hardware, where the margins are not so large.

