DWasser@mdf.com (David Wasser) writes:

>We are looking for a cross-platform development environment for VMS, UNIX,
>WinNT and OS/2. This should be a graphical IDE which supports (at least) C.
>Since there seem to be no products on the market which do this, we may
>be forced to settle for a less-than-optimal solution (ie: one which does
>not fulfill all our requirements).

>Before deciding, we want to get feedback from anyonw who has some experience
>with such tools.

>Please post all information, suggestions, horror-stories, product reviews,
>etc. either to this newsgroup or (better still) email me at <DWasser@mdf.com>.

You'll have quite a challenge finding something that matches _all_ the environments.
It really depends on what you're trying to develop.  I have experience with
DEC's VMS development tools and the out-of-the-box UNIX tools.  Neither are
GUI interfaced.  DEC's products worked with all of DEC products.  Howerver,
VMS is _not_ Unix, despite what DEC will tell you.  exec() and fork() did not
exist in V5 (they may have added it to some release of V6) and code which
works just fine on Unix systems won't work on VMS.  Can't say much about NT
or OS/2, except you'll probably have a Microsoft product there.

Good luck,

