I believe it's impossible due to the size of the Ultrix kernel.
Apart from that the floppy drive (assuming it's a RX23) is a SCSI
device as any other.  I don�t think non-SCSI floppy drives are
possible with a DS5000.  If there is a 2.8MB-variant (similar to
the NeXT floppy drives) then you might be able to squeeze a
absolutely minimal kernel on that.

So, what do you need to get the system working at all ?

/dev/*
/bin/ls
/bin/mount
/bin/sh
/etc/init (though I'm not sure about the location on Ultrix)
/etc/rc (possibly empty)
/etc/termcap (stripped to dumb/vt100 and a few more)
/etc/ttys
/ultrixboot
/vmunix

I guess you're very lucky if you succeed in doing that...

