Hi all,

I've some difficulties in installing NT 3.5.1 on an AlphaStation 255/233
with a PBXGB graphics option (Cirrus Logic chipset).

The machine came with VMS preinstalled and has been in use with VMS for
a few months. DEC did not recommend to use NT 4.0 right now, so we
purchased the NT 3.5.1 OEM package from DEC, which comes along with DEC
floppies and CDs, including support for the AlphaStation 255, but no
graphics drivers. (This software is also available from the DEC web
site, as well as the firmware update. I also had to download AlphaBIOS
firmware, since this particular machine did not come with a firmware CD)

When trying to install NT, and defining VGA as graphic mode,
installation aborts with 
  STOP C0000143 [Missing system file] Required system file
  DISLPAY_DRIVER.SYS is bad or missing.

I then searched Usenet, the DEC Web-Site, Microsoft Knowledge Base (MS
KB) and the Cirrus Logic Web-Site.

From a hint in comp.sys.dec with a similar problen, on a different model
though, and a related hint from MS KB, I copied the Alpha\Cirrus video
driver files from the NT-CD to a floppy disk and chose the
"Other"-option when defining video hardware during installation.

Now I no longer get the STOP 143-message after rebooting, instead I get
a *black* screen. Disk access continues for a while afterwards and
that's been it - toggle power switch.

I tried to download drivers from Cirrus Logic for the GD5424 chipset
(Could they work at all on Alpha?), but this trial failed quite early
with an error message "missing <configname>..." when attempting to read
the floppy disk.

What I also did: I reset the frequency switch on the PBXGB graphics
board back to pos C, 640x480, 60 Hz instead of 0, 1280 x 1024, 72 Hz,
used for VMS. The owner's manual says, the switch is not used at all for
NT, but who knows. Well, the switch position didn't matter anyway. 

I don't have a "Graphics Support Services Software Version 3.0 for
Microsoft Windows NT Installation and User Guide", maybe it's not
shipped with a VMS version. Did I miss anything from this manual?

