X-Deja-AN: 203871173
references: <32b169a5.64647768@SantaClara01.news.internex.net>
content-type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=ISO-8859-1
organization: ICL Data Oy
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.sys.dec.micro


FX!32 is for running Intel Win32 binaries under Windows NT 4.0 on
Alpha systems, and doesn't apply to DOS programs (built with or
without a DOS extender).

With DOS programs, you're running under the built-in Virtual DOS 
Machine (or VDM) on Windows NT (and in the case of Windows NT 4.0 
it means i486 emulation on RISC platforms, whereas on earlier 
Windows NT releases it meant Intel 80286 emulation, which excluded 
apps built using 32-bit DOS extenders).

In general, I don't know about DOS apps handling dongles under Windows NT
(regardless whether the hardware platform is RISC or Intel). Windows NT
disallows all direct hardware access, and for DOS programs the dongle
would have to be accessed via support MS-DOS and/or BIOS interfaces in
order for it to work (or, should I say, for the application to work ;-).

regards,
...petri (petri.backstrom@icl.fi)
   ICL Data Oy
   Finland

