I have an Emulex UC07 in my uVAX 3600 and it works flawlessly with my
old Quantum Empire 2 Gb SCSI drive.

My setup:
	KDA650-AA
	MS650-AA	(4x == 32 Mb)
	DELQA-SA
	UC07
	TQK70
	KDA50 (with RA82 attached)

The drive, however is begnning to show signs of wear (bad blocks) 
so I'm looking for a replacement.

I got a brand-new IBM DORS 32160 2.1Gb drive and hooked it up to
the Emulex. Using the on-board FRD I can format, verify and
do a reliability test on the drive OK, but when I try to boot off 
it (B DUB0:) the only thing I get is 'DEVOFFLINE' when it should 
complain about a non-existing boot-block...

It seems like the IBM drive either expects a bit more from the controller
or send extra SENSE info which confuses the UC07, because I do see
the activity LED on the UC07 flash briefly..

Now.. I'm not really trying to find out what's going wrong here, because 
I'm afraid I won't be able to change very much about it, but I just 
wanted to see if anyone else has seen the same effect on their UC07/08.

What (recent) big-capacity (2-4 Gb) drives are you guys hooking up to
Emulex boards?

I can trade this drive in for a 2 Gb HP drive so I'll try that as well...

