newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


The DECpc 433 Workstation (a.k.a. 433W, codename "Eclipse") has
a built in Ethernet adapter based on the old DE100 (DEC EtherWORKS
LC, a.k.a. DEPCA-LC) design.

The remote boot it supports is based on the MOP (Maintenance
Operations Protocol), and a PATHWORKS server (VMS, Digital UNIX)
does how to respond (in order to boot DOS/Windows 3.x with PATHWORKS
support).

PATHWORKS V5 servers and later redirect the MOP boot to a LAN Manager
RIPL (=RPL), Remote Initial Program Load boot.

Lanworks Technologies (a Canadian company), if my memory serves me
right, has a BOOTP (or maybe just RPL) ROM chip for the DE100; search 
the web (http://altavista.digital.com) for sure. 

I remember also a German company (circa 1991) doing a BOOTP ROM for 
the EtherWORKS 2 boards.

The Token Ring variant of the DECpc 433W has an Olicom design 
Token Ring adapter built-in. I don't remember if it had built-in
remote boot support, but Olicom might have a boot ROM for it.

regards,
...petri (petri.backstrom@icl.fi)
