Linux is under development. I currently have the timer interrupt working on
my DS5000/200. Take a look at http://www.softway.com.au/~paul/dec/
for further information on the Linux port. It's still far from being usable.

You can currently get a version of NetBSD for the DS5000 or try to find an 
Ultrix/RISC license from DEC.

: 	DecStation 5000/200 Model PM36A-DG

MIPS R3000 CPU, 25 MHz.

: 	2 Memory cards, one marked A01 ZG12648170
: 			one marked A01 ZG12748261

Should be 16 MB RAM.

: 	PMAG-D/PXG Video card, marked C08 AB11403XBB
: 	with some memory on a daughter card marked
: 			B01 ZG10521108

Some accelerated video card, if I'm not mistaken. 

Re. the connectors:
The DS5000/200 has 2 RS232 ports, a single-ended SCSI port, 10Base2 Ethernet 
and a keyboard/mouse interface.

This machine is probably worth around US$300-$500.

Hope this helps,
regards,
