that other than use at educational institutions violoated the terms
of the UNIX license agreement.

The book only covers the kernel by the way, so you've still got a long
way to go.  I don't know if it has the assembly parts either (I'm not
sure I konw where mine is anymore).

Much as I was a fan of PDP-11's in their day (I continued to recycle
them
into internet routers after the UNIX usefulness was over), V6 UNIX isn't
going to be a whole lot of fun.  Relatively tiny file ssytems and even
smaller memory limits.  You'd be better off with a hot copy of the later
2BSD's...



