I've upgraded an AlphaStation 400 from Windows NT Workstation 3.5 to
4.0 and may have seen the same problem. It turned out to be a pilot
error.

If I remember correctly, I had to install the video drivers from a
floppy disk coming with the system when I installed 3.5. During the
upgrade, the installation procedure told me that the video drivers
(TGA.SYS and TGA.DLL ?) were not those supplied with the 3.5 kit and
asked whether I wanted to keep them or whether I wanted to use the new
ones from the 4.0 CD-ROM.
I erroneously replied 'keep' and after the next reboot, the
AlphaStation crashed complaining about DISPLAY_DRIVER.DLL.

I restarted the upgrade, this time chose to use the new TGA.* files
and the upgrade finished without (major) problems. Only SERIAL.INI for
the RAS Server was missing...

Hope this helps,

