Well, 

I have just spent time getting HylaFAX to work under ULTRIX 4.3A with
fax class 2 (not 2.0) modems hung off terminal server ports DECserver
90TLs and 90Ms.

Talk about massochism!

I have also figured out how to munge a MS Word produced cover page (as
a postscript file) so it can be used for the Cover Page template that
HylaFAX uses. This approach allows one to use the local company logo
as used on all Word documents, and works well with HylaFAX.

I will put up a web page on the details one day about how to do it
all, but briefly:

1. Configure terminal server ports for: 19200, no flow control, access
remote and use lcp or latcp (on DU) to point a /dev/ttynn device at
term-server and port:

  lcp -h ttynn:SERV:PORT

2. Configure HylaFAX for the modem and the term server setup in the
config.ttynn file in HylaFAX etc directory with xonxoff flow control
but with wait for XON before sending data as no.

HylaFAX is very robust and seems to be able to drive multiple modems
at the same time and to spread load across them all.
