>   replace a P133 chip with a P150 chip in the same system...It makes perfect
>   sense that it would run slower?  Can somebody help me out with this?
>			   Bill Thomas

As I understand it, the P150 systems typically run the board at 30 Mhz
(CPU is 5x the board clock), whereas the P133 run it at 33 (CPU 4x the
board).  So for operations that are dependent on memory access speeds,
the P133 is often faster due to its 10% faster board speed.

For the record, I have a Starion 930 (P100) and have been relatively
happy with it.  Most of my problems have ended up being bugs in Win95.
I have had to upgrade various drivers a times (they're available from
the Digital PC web site).

