I haven't tried compiling the simulator yet,  but if you want to recode it for
DOS instead of UNIX, it should be possible with the usual degree of difficulty
in making this kind of port.

The RDOS available is the DG Nova operating system, and was posted to run with
the simulator. It will not be of any help to you.

Whatever simulator you run will *probably* be slower than the original
machine,  and will require a great deal of expansion to handle real-world I/O,
especially the kind demanded by scientific devices.

And no matter what kind of machine you use, a change will probably mean
building or obtaining all sorts of new I/O hardware.

You really have two choices: new code for a new machine or a repair for your
PDP-11 (alternatively a replacement for your -11) Given the number of -11s
produced and the numbers cited for used beasts, repairing the PDP-11,
especially if the system does everything you want it to, is probably the best
solution.

