I looked in my users manual and saw where there were supposed to be
jumpers on the motherboard that would allow you to upgrade the CPU from
the P75 up to the P100. Guess what ? The jumpers were removed and
soldered over. The customer service people didn't have an explanation.
BTW, my Starion, being one of the early models, actually had the 3-year
warranty with parts & labor. Later models had parts & labor the first
year and parts only for the remaining 2.



