Hi,	
	Thanks to everyone who responded to my post.  Now that we know we're not
alone, and that these Starion problems are NOT isolated cases, its time we
do something about it.  What steps we take next...I'm not sure, but for
those of you who want to know exactly what I did to get Digital to replace
my telecommander and mother board, I've written out below, the steps I took
(with some ranting in between :)):
	The first thing I did was call customer service... a lot!  Since our
problems can't be fixed over the phone, I knew I had to speak with someone
besides customer service. I then got a # for customer RELATIONS  The # is
1-800-215-8768  I spoke with a guy named Bruce Ginsburg ext. 501 (sorry
Bruce)  He was the first Digital rep that admitted they were aware of the
Telecommander problem and that they have been replacing telecommanders with
SB16's and U.S. Robotics 28.8's.. (actually he was the second, the first
was the tech that came to my house and installed 2 defective Telecommanders
in my system.  He said he installs new Telecommanders everyday, this was
about 6-7 months ago).  So Bruce was the guy who authorized replacement.  I
had to: fax Bruce a copy of the receipt from the purchase of the computer,
bring my computer to CompUSA, pay for the parts and labor,  then mail/fax
the receipt to Bruce.  I received money back within a week.
	This didn't fix the speed problem.  It just fixed some windows/DOS
problems.  Quake runs better in win 95 now.  Doesn't get stuck at Sound
initialization screen anymore.
	After all that aggravation I took a break for about a month.  Still
getting poor performance I decided to upgrade my video.  I bought a 4MB
Matrox Millenium.  But, of coarse, it didn't give the 25% increase I needed
to bring me up to speed.  I knew this before buying it , but more than 1
tech support person told me my problem was the 1 MB of video I have. 
WRONG.  
	Still not ready to start pursuing Digital again I decided to install one
of the new Verite based 3D cards so at least Quake would run at a decent
speed.  Don't bother trying this, the cards don't work in our Starions. 
None of the games that came with the card worked, even funnier yet, none of
my games worked, even the ones that don't use verite enhancement.  Games
would boot up then crash to black screen  I called the manufacturer of the
card, Intergraph, after giving me a few suggestions that didn't work they
recommended I take them up on their 14 day return policy.  I did.  THANKS
AGAIN DIGITAL.
	This really pissed me off and I started in with Digital again.  I called
Bruce again, he was on vacation.  I spoke to someone else in the same
office as him, Customer relations.  He said that his office doesn't deal
with Starion problems.  I told him that Bruce helped me out with my modem,
and he said "well, thats different"!? then gave me the 800-554-3333
customer service #.  Whatever.
	When I called this # I told them about the poor benchmark results and told
them of all of the visits from there tech guy with the Telecommander.  I
let them know that I tried every benchmark program available on the
internet that I could find.  All of them gave me poor results. 
Winbench96-97, Wintune96, Bench96, Norton SI, they all said I was running
30-50% slower than comparable systems.  I let them know that I tried
reinstalling to factory settings with no improvement.  I told them I
reinstalled, from scratch, windows 95 alone, still no improvement.  They
asked if I installed my 2nd hard drive correctly.  I opened up the computer
answered their questions, its installed correctly.  They thought that maybe
I got a defective CPU.  So they came to my house and replaced it, didn't
work.  The same person came back with a new motherboard, this was last
week, no improvement.  Basically what this tells us all, is that this is
not a case of a few defective motherboards here and there.  The only way
that our computers will run at the speed they were ADVERTISED as doing,
(the tech that came to my house told me that the "as advertised" statement
is the key.), is to rig our computers with faster processors, just to get
what we paid for.  In other words, put a P150 in place of my P133 just to
get the performance of a P133.  And this is exactly what Digital has done. 

	In a couple of hours the tech should be here with my Starion 950
motherboard, which has a P150 chip.  If this doesn't bring me up to speed
I'm going to demand that they install the Starion 960 motherboard which has
a P166.  I have a funny feeling this is what I'll be doing. :)
	So this is what I've done so far, I hope this helps you.
	Stay tuned for more
						Bill Thomas




