Hi Everyone,
	The Digital tech just left my house.  She installed the 950 motherboard
and P150 chip in my 940.  Guess what...It ran SLOWER!  I tried to run one
of the tests in Winbench 97 and the machine would freeze up.  We had to
reset.  Tried a couple more times...same thing.  I ran Quake's timerefresh
test...I lost 2 fps...down from 20 to 18.  Well we both burst out laughing.
	She then called Digital (can you believe she doesn't have a special # she
can call...she has to call the same customer service # that we do AND wait
on hold)  The person that she spoke to said the 950 motherboard will not
work in the 940.  The tech than proceeded to say "why the hell did you
order this part and have me install it then?" The person on the other end
did not have an answer to that!  Can you believe this?
	The tech that was here at my house has been working for Digital for 15
years.  She just transferred here (California) from Oklahoma 2 months ago. 
Since shes been here she has worked on... Starions... and only...Starions. 
She also mentioned Digital should have never entered the home PC market "it
was the dumbest thing they've done since she has been working for them"
	So I got on the phone with the person we were speaking to.  I told her and
the tech told her also, that theres nothing else that can be done for this
machine.  Its so rigged up were going in reverse now.  And that the only
thing that can be done at this point is to give me my money back, or send
me a completely different computer, NO STARIONS!  I believe the Celebris FX
is the only computer they make now that you can get with Win 95.  She said
that she couldn't make a decision like that and that I would have to call
Customer Satisfaction dept. 1-405-762-8719 :)  I called the # and got the
recording that all reps are busy and to 'leave a message' It was 2:15 here
in Cali so it was 5:15 in New Hampshire. I guess everyone went home.
	Well the next week should be very exciting.  I'm expecting a call from
them tomorrow...Stay tuned:)
					Bill Thomas
	



