Luke H. Shepherd (lshep@nr.infi.net) wrote:
: I am wondering how other sites assure the time is the same on all VAX 
: nodes on the network.
[...]
: We do not run TCP/IP on any of the nodes.  I 
: have found various NTP-TCP/IP servers on the markets.  The WWV port and 
: information is sometimes unreliable.

My company sells a product named TMS (Time Management System). It sets the
system clock by adjusting the time ticks, so that the system time is set in
a smooth way (important for our outher business - measurement values
processing). It receives time information from some radio controlled clock
(called DCF77 in Europe - for which I fear are the only drivers we offer
now), but it can also use some other VAXen's system time received via
DECnet or TCP/IP. Have a look at our WWW site at www.pdv-systeme.de or
contact info@pdv-systeme.de via E-Mail.

