The C & E News article probably dated from about 1981 or 1982, as
I recall reading it while I was in grad school.  The article showed
a picture of a firefighter spraying halon from a hose -- perfhaps
not the same bore as a conventional water hose, but more substantial
than the average fire extinguisher.  The fire department in
question was in the northern middle of the US, and I believe
the non-icing aspect of the halon was also desirable.

