newsgroups: comp.sys.dec



I used to have an RO204, and documentation.  Of course,
those are long since gone, but I do remember one thing about
the drives that I found "unusual" enough to remember:

On one of the boards, where the motor/servo leads go into the drive 
itself, there should be a SMALL wire "jumper" installed.  Right next to
it is a set of pads, where another jumper could be installed.

If you can find this jumper, it is for the hall-effect sensor, inside
the drive.  Apparently, Rodime was worried enough that this sensor
might fail, and designed it with TWO sensors.  Cutting this jumper,
and soldering another one on the pads NEXT TO IT, enables the other
hall sensor.  This *MIGHT* be your problem.

It couldn't hurt to try. . .


Tim Thompson (Formerly of Milwaukee fame. . .)

