Use the standard 4mm DAT driver that ships with Windows NT. It will
work just fine. The TLZ06 also has a "reserved" jumper (7 or 8, I 
don't remember which ;-) that will - if the tape drive's firmware
is recent enough (I don't remember the revision either ;-) - make
the drive report itself as an Archive Python instead of a Digital
TLZ06.

Digital Customer Services should be able to supply you with a tape
that has the latest firmware (you upgrade by just powering on the
drive and inserting the tape; the drive will eject the tape when
the upgrade is complete).

