   Interesting theory - however I'm not sure the history of Digital memory
prices bears it out.

   I have used 3rd party memory in a variety of DEC systems over the last
20 years and have never found it to be any less reliable than DECs. I've
also never seen any research which indicates this to be the case ( and
I'm sure if such research existed DEC would be trumpeting from the rooftops)

   I have no experience with this particular system, however if you look
at the Digital memory prices for any system you will find they are far
above "commodity" prices. When they are in fact selling "commodity" parts
(eg SIMMs) they will charge 2-3 times the street price - for custom
modules 8-10x premiums seem more the norm. I got burned by this recently,
having to buy DEC memory for an AS 2100 at about $50/MB ( and *that* was
for a refurbished module, new modules were something like $75/MB ). OTOH
my AS 1000A uses SIMMS and I can pick up reliable, brand-name memory for
it for about $10-15/MB (using 64Mbit parts)

