Brian, has the port of the DECserver been setup properly?  I ask because
you didn't mention it in your post.

1. LATCP on the host side creates the LTA device
2. SET TERM on the host side sets some of the LTA device
characteristics, however keep in mind that not many of them matter.  Two
that always cause problems are parity and character size.
3. NCP CONNECT NODE or TSM to access the DECserver and setup the port.
ACCESS must be REMOTE and there's a bunch of other stuff you'll need to
worry about there.

By my count you missed #3.



